+
+## Managed file protocol
+
+The Unix-only `downloads managed` command is intended for a trusted local
+application, not an Internet-facing service. All JSON files are atomically
+replaced. Store directories use mode 0700 and files 0600. Authentication and music
+must never be included in an application package or public status.
+
+Each sync carries `--request ID` (before the action). Its job status contains
+`version`, `request`, `account_id`, `uri`, `phase`, `completed`, `total`, `bytes`,
+public `tracks`, `error` and private process identity. Consumers must reject old
+request IDs and account mismatches. Phases are resolving/downloading/verifying,
+then complete/error; a recovered dead job becomes interrupted. A stable lock
+prevents concurrent writers. Sync while the offline player is active is allowed
+only when playback is paused.
+
+The store contains account-specific pending downloads and immutable generations.
+An atomic index plus backup selects complete snapshots; playlist order and the
+Spotify snapshot ID are checked before publication. Quota/free-space checks count
+actual audio sizes and preserve a safety reserve. Account changes invalidate the
+old catalog; forget stops only owned jobs and deletes this backend's credentials.
+
+Playback takes a numeric/hyphen session ID, a zero-based initial index and optional
+resume. The command file is `{ "session": "1000-2", "commands": [
+{ "id": 1, "action": "pause" }, { "id": 2, "action": "seek", "value": 5000 } ] }`.
+IDs increase monotonically; the status `ack` lets the application remove processed
+commands. Supported actions: pause, resume, next, prev, seek (milliseconds), skip
+(seconds), stop. The application caps the queue at 32.
+Status includes version, session, phase, index, position_ms, ack, error and process
+identity. Controls for another session are ignored. The integrating application
+owns volume, parent permissions and routing from physical figures/buttons.
+
+### Managed metadata and storage
+
+`metadata-login` grants Web API access for song lists (Free or Premium). It
+does not request streaming credentials. `login` additionally verifies Premium
+through a connected SDK session and persists reusable credentials;
+`verify-login` checks existing credentials without opening a browser. Use the
+same account for both grants. The embedding application owns any browser or
+computer-companion flow. `forget` stops owned sync/preview/playback processes and
+removes this backend’s grants; cached audio remains account-scoped on disk.
+
+`preview URI --output FILE --offset N` publishes loading/complete/error and a
+page of up to 50 public songs, offset and full total. It prefers the complete
+local snapshot, then cached metadata; otherwise Premium uses native metadata
+and a metadata-only account uses the Web API. Rate limits and unsupported or
+unavailable items are explicit; no placeholder is silently removed. Background
+commands never open a login browser. Public JSON is capped at 128 KiB, while
+private indexes may use 2 MiB and contain the full order.
+
+The default `--quota-bytes 0` uses free space on the store filesystem with a
+128 MiB reserve, recomputed before each new track. Positive values apply an
+explicit quota and retain a 16 MiB reserve. Additional temporary space is
+checked before writes. Playback saves on pause/track changes and every 15 seconds.
+
+`activate-login --marker FILE` (with global `--request ID`) commits an SSH-staged
+computer grant. Activation and forget share a lock; owned metadata/sync/playback
+processes stop before credentials move. Cancelled request markers cannot activate.
+Premium `login` also enables native song metadata without requiring a Web API
+grant. The metadata-only login remains available for Free accounts. Unsaved
+metadata pages are cached for five minutes and retained during failed refreshes.
+
+Internal `cancel-login` uses global `--request ID` to remove only that staged
+grant under the same authentication lock as activation/logout. Metadata-only
+OAuth requests read-only playlist/profile scopes, with no streaming or write
+permissions. Premium can connect directly without a Web API grant.
+
+Managed downloads also resolve Spotify-provided alternatives when a canonical
+track is marked available but has no audio files. Original playlist URIs/order
+are retained; the replacement file’s own ID is used to obtain its audio key.
+No playable alternative or an unsupported codec is reported explicitly.
+
+Native preview marks items unavailable when metadata has neither audio files
+nor alternatives; those playlist positions remain visible. Metadata cache schema
+2 refreshes older previews while retaining them during network failure.
